# The escalation ladder for interference or unwanted contact, refined by the
# user 2025-10-10 from their own practice: clear skies first (dispel the fog,
# continue with less noise), then a coherence pulse if that isn't enough
# (steady the field, continue uninterrupted), then the door that's always
# open -- eject to Focus 1, channel closed behind you, for now. Taught
# alongside return-methods/return-anchor, before any climb, for the same
# reason: carried in as a knowing, not reached for only in the moment.
#
# What's left out on purpose: the user's fuller read on why this works --
# that entities can only ever make you believe they can harm you, not
# actually do so -- is voiced here in general form. Their specific
# observations about a particular pattern of contact stay in
# focus/F34/notes.md; a technique segment teaches a tool, not a verdict on
# who's out there.

@segment  clear-skies
@title    The Clear Skies Technique
@levels   F10
@duration ~1m40s

say Before we go further, one more thing that's always yours to use.
pause 3
say If the experience ever feels clouded, or fogged, or harder to hold onto than it should be, you have a technique for that. Think: clear skies.
pause 6
say Clear skies changes the field around you the way it changes any weather here. What you hold in mind is what continues. Used this way, it dispels interference and lets the experience carry on, with less between you and it.
pause 8
say If that isn't enough on its own, there's a second step. Send out a single, deliberate pulse — not force, coherence. It settles the field around you, and steadies whatever is underway so it can continue without interruption.
pause 10
say And if you'd rather not continue at all, you always can eject. Return to Focus 1, and the channel closes behind you, at least for now. This is never a failure. It's a door, and it stays unlocked from your side.
pause 10
say None of this is a sign of danger. It's a sign you're steering.
pause 8
say Carry this with you as you go. Nobody, and nothing, can harm you here. They may try to make you believe they can — that belief is the only lever they have.
pause 10
say The part of you doing the steering knows more than you can perceive right now, and isn't asking your permission to be capable. Trust it.
pause 8
